<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> PPO with Pruning and Optional SA Regularization</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          Initial policy parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>; Pruning masks <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each layer (initialized as all ones, i.e. no pruning applied);
Adversarial budget <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(s)</annotation></semantics></math> (state perturbation set);
Regularization weight <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
Total update horizon <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>;
Burn-in fraction <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>;
Choice of pruning rule.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          Initialize update counter <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each update iteration <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            Collect trajectories using adversarial states <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{s}\in B(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{s}\in B(s)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute advantages <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and returns <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each minibatch <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
             Compute PPO loss with SA regularisation
<math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{PPO}}+\kappa\,\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}(\theta;\mathcal{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>PPO</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{PPO}}+\kappa\,\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}(\theta;\mathcal{B})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
             Update network parameters with gradient descent

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t/T&gt;\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t/T&gt;\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (network burn-in) <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
               Update pruning masks <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> according to chosen rule

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
               Apply masks to network parameters <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> pruning step
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (SA-MDP robustness improves under pruning). ‣ 3.2 Performance–robustness trade-offs ‣ 3 Robustness Bounds in SA-MDPs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For any policy <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and its optimal adversary <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{*}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{*}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> in the state-adversarial MDP (SA-MDP), it holds from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., [2020]</a></cite> that</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{s}\big\{V^{\pi}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\pi\circ\nu^{*}(\pi)}(s)\big\}\;\leq\;\alpha\max_{s}\max_{\hat{s}\in B(s)}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\big(\pi(\cdot|s),\pi(\cdot|\hat{s})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>α</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>s</mi></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{s}\big\{V^{\pi}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\pi\circ\nu^{*}(\pi)}(s)\big\}\;\leq\;\alpha\max_{s}\max_{\hat{s}\in B(s)}D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\big(\pi(\cdot|s),\pi(\cdot|\hat{s})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(s)=\{\,\hat{s}:\|\hat{s}-s\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(s)=\{\,\hat{s}:\|\hat{s}-s\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon\,\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> perturbation ball, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes total variation distance.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Network Lipschitz bound.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the policy network be an <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layer feedforward model with parameters <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\{W_{1},\dots,W_{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\{W_{1},\dots,W_{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, biases <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\sigma_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\sigma_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>–Lipschitz activations <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Explicitly, the network map <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the function composition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{\theta}(s)\;=\;W_{L}\,\sigma_{L-1}\!\Big(W_{L-1}\,\sigma_{L-2}\big(\cdots\sigma_{1}(W_{1}s+b_{1})+b_{L-1}\big)\Big)+b_{L}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(s)\;=\;W_{L}\,\sigma_{L-1}\!\Big(W_{L-1}\,\sigma_{L-2}\big(\cdots\sigma_{1}(W_{1}s+b_{1})+b_{L-1}\big)\Big)+b_{L},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied elementwise. Biases do not affect Lipschitz constants.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz constant of a linear map <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto W_{\ell}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto W_{\ell}x</annotation></semantics></math> is its operator (spectral) norm <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, since</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{\ell}x-W_{\ell}y\|_{2}=\|W_{\ell}(x-y)\|_{2}\leq\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{\ell}x-W_{\ell}y\|_{2}=\|W_{\ell}(x-y)\|_{2}\leq\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus the Lipschitz constant of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(f_{\theta})\;\leq\;\Bigg(\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}L_{\sigma_{\ell}}\Bigg)\,\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(f_{\theta})\;\leq\;\Bigg(\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}L_{\sigma_{\ell}}\Bigg)\,\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since computing or constraining <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be difficult, we introduce monotone surrogates. For any matrix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{2}\;\leq\;\|A\|_{F},\qquad\|A\|_{2}\;\leq\;\sqrt{\|A\|_{1}\,\|A\|_{\infty}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{2}\;\leq\;\|A\|_{F},\qquad\|A\|_{2}\;\leq\;\sqrt{\|A\|_{1}\,\|A\|_{\infty}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">These upper bounds are monotone in the entries of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, hence suitable for analyzing pruning. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(f_{\theta})\;\leq\;\Bigg(\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}L_{\sigma_{\ell}}\Bigg)\,\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\min\!\Big\{\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{F},\;\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}\|_{\infty}}\,\Big\}=:\tilde{L}_{\theta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(f_{\theta})\;\leq\;\Bigg(\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}L_{\sigma_{\ell}}\Bigg)\,\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\min\!\Big\{\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{F},\;\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}\|_{\infty}}\,\Big\}=:\tilde{L}_{\theta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus for any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,\hat{s}\in B(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,\hat{s}\in B(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\theta}(\hat{s})-f_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\theta}(\hat{s})-f_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gaussian policies.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a|s)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\theta}(s),\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a|s)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\theta}(s),\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the closed-form total variation distance between Gaussians with equal covariance gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\hat{s})\big)\;\leq\;\frac{\|\mu_{\theta}(\hat{s})-\mu_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\hat{s})\big)\;\leq\;\frac{\|\mu_{\theta}(\hat{s})-\mu_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Categorical policies.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s)=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s)=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta}(s))</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-partition function is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, which yields the standard bound</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\hat{s}))\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\,\|z_{\theta}(s)-z_{\theta}(\hat{s})\|_{2}\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\hat{s}))\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\,\|z_{\theta}(s)-z_{\theta}(\hat{s})\|_{2}\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Effect of pruning.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be obtained by elementwise pruning, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\ell}^{\prime}=\mathcal{M}_{\ell}\odot W_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\ell}^{\prime}=\mathcal{M}_{\ell}\odot W_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> with binary masks <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each surrogate norm is monotone under pruning:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{F}\leq\|W_{\ell}\|_{F},\qquad\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}}\;\leq\;\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}\|_{\infty}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{F}\leq\|W_{\ell}\|_{F},\qquad\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}}\;\leq\;\sqrt{\|W_{\ell}\|_{1}\|W_{\ell}\|_{\infty}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\leq\tilde{L}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\leq\tilde{L}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Activation Lipschitz constants are unchanged, so the same bounds apply with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is no larger.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for Gaussian (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and categorical (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>) policies,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{s}\{V^{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\circ\nu^{*}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})}(s)\}\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\,\varepsilon\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>s</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{s}\{V^{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(s)-\tilde{V}^{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\circ\nu^{*}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})}(s)\}\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\,\varepsilon\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta}\,\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus pruning cannot worsen the certified robustness bound.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tightness of the bound.</span>
The surrogate Lipschitz bound <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> from Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (SA-MDP robustness improves under pruning). ‣ 3.2 Performance–robustness trade-offs ‣ 3 Robustness Bounds in SA-MDPs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> is guaranteed to be
monotone under entrywise pruning, but it can be loose compared to the
true sensitivity of the policy. A sharper, distribution–dependent refinement is
given in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Local robustness bound). ‣ Effect of pruning. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\,\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon))\;\leq\;c\Big(\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\epsilon+\tfrac{1}{2}\beta\,\epsilon^{2}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\,\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon))\;\leq\;c\Big(\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\epsilon+\tfrac{1}{2}\beta\,\epsilon^{2}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a curvature constant capturing the local variation of the Jacobian,
e.g. an upper bound on the Lipschitz constant of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{g_{\theta}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{g_{\theta}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. This local bound is (trivially)
always no larger than the global bound (exact for ReLU networks, up to an
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> term otherwise), and often much tighter since typical Jacobians have small operator norm. However,
unlike <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is not guaranteed to decrease monotonically under
pruning. Thus, the global bound provides provable monotone improvement,
while the local refinement better reflects the true robustness landscape but may vary non-monotonically.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local robustness bound)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be either a Gaussian policy
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\theta}(s),\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\theta}(s),\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>
with fixed <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
or a categorical policy
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s)=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s)=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta}(s))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose the network outputs <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>
(mean <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> or logits <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\theta}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\theta}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>) are <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, i.e.,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{g_{\theta}}(x)-J_{g_{\theta}}(y)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\beta\|x-y\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{g_{\theta}}(x)-J_{g_{\theta}}(y)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\beta\|x-y\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any perturbation <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and state <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\,\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\;\leq\;c\Big(\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\,\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\;\leq\;c\Big(\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{g_{\theta}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{g_{\theta}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Jacobian of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (operator norm induced by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}</annotation></semantics></math> for Gaussians and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math> for categoricals.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By first-order Taylor’s theorem with integral remainder and the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)=g_{\theta}(s)+J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\,\epsilon+\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}\!\big(J_{g_{\theta}}(s+t\epsilon)-J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\big)\,\epsilon\,\mathrm{d}t}_{r(\epsilon)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)=g_{\theta}(s)+J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\,\epsilon+\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}\!\big(J_{g_{\theta}}(s+t\epsilon)-J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\big)\,\epsilon\,\mathrm{d}t}_{r(\epsilon)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r(\epsilon)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s+t\epsilon)-J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\|\epsilon\|_{2}\,\mathrm{d}t\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\beta\,t\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}t\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r(\epsilon)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s+t\epsilon)-J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\|\epsilon\|_{2}\,\mathrm{d}t\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\beta\,t\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}t\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-g_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-g_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\|J_{g_{\theta}}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\beta\,\|\epsilon\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For Gaussians with identical covariance <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the closed-form total variation bound gives
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\leq\|\,\mu_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-\mu_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}/\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\leq\|\,\mu_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-\mu_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}/\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}.</annotation></semantics></math>
For categoricals, the softmax log-partition is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, yielding
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\leq\tfrac{1}{4}\|\,z_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-z_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s+\epsilon)\big)\leq\tfrac{1}{4}\|\,z_{\theta}(s+\epsilon)-z_{\theta}(s)\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Applying these with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> as the mean or logits respectively establishes the claim.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Unified regret under SA attack). ‣ 3.2 Performance–robustness trade-offs ‣ 3 Robustness Bounds in SA-MDPs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected robustness gap)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any start-state distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s_{0}\sim\mu}[V_{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{0})-\tilde{V}_{\pi_{\theta}\circ\nu^{*}}(s_{0})]\;\leq\;\alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\!\big[TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\big]\;\leq\;\mathcal{B}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s_{0}\sim\mu}[V_{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{0})-\tilde{V}_{\pi_{\theta}\circ\nu^{*}}(s_{0})]\;\leq\;\alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\!\big[TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\big]\;\leq\;\mathcal{B}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first inequality is obtained from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., [2020]</a></cite> by taking the expectation over the difference in values instead of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="max_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">max_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The constant <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (defined in the main paper) collects the reward bound and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the second inequality, note that by definition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\;\leq\;TV_{\max}(s;\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\;\leq\;TV_{\max}(s;\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectations over <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s}\Big[TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\Big]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}_{s}\big[TV_{\max}(s;\theta)\big]=F(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s}\Big[TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid s),\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\nu^{*}(s)))\Big]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}_{s}\big[TV_{\max}(s;\theta)\big]=F(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Multiplying by <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> gives the claimed bound <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(\theta)=\alpha F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(\theta)=\alpha F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Clean/attacked value drop under pruning). ‣ B.3 Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Clean/attacked value drop under pruning)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be Gaussian with fixed covariance <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> or categorical softmax with logits <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\theta}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\theta}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> from a Lipschitz network.
Assume that for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\mapsto g_{\phi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\mapsto g_{\phi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable almost everywhere.
For any pruned parameters <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}=\theta-\Delta\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}=\theta-\Delta\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}^{\mathrm{par}}_{\phi}:=\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\|J_{\phi}g_{\phi}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\Big)^{1/2},\qquad\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\int_{0}^{1}\hat{L}^{\mathrm{par}}_{\theta^{\prime}+t(\theta-\theta^{\prime})}\,\mathrm{d}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>par</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>par</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>par</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}^{\mathrm{par}}_{\phi}:=\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\|J_{\phi}g_{\phi}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\Big)^{1/2},\qquad\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\int_{0}^{1}\hat{L}^{\mathrm{par}}_{\theta^{\prime}+t(\theta-\theta^{\prime})}\,\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}=\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}=\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> for Gaussian and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\tfrac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\tfrac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}=z_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}=z_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> for categorical, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|,\qquad\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>par</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>par</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|,\qquad\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\;\leq\;\alpha\,c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Here <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> on parameters is Euclidean, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the operator norm induced by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the SA–MDP value–difference bound (Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Expected robustness gap). ‣ B.2 Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> in TV form) applied to two policies at the same state,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\;\leq\;\alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\Big[\,TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\;\leq\;\alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\mu}^{\pi_{\theta}}}\Big[\,TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gaussian:</span> For Gaussians with identical covariance <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the closed-form TV bound is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\;\leq\;\frac{\|\mu_{\theta}(s)-\mu_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\;\leq\;\frac{\|\mu_{\theta}(s)-\mu_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}}{\sqrt{2\pi\,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Categorical:</span> For <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\mathrm{softmax}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\mathrm{softmax}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-partition is <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, yielding</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s))\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\|z_{\theta}(s)-z_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s))\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{4}\|z_{\theta}(s)-z_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, in both cases,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\;\leq\;c\,\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mpadded style="width:0.636em;" width="0.636em"><mi>V</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\!\big(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s),\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot|s)\big)\;\leq\;c\,\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now let <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t):=\theta^{\prime}+t(\theta-\theta^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t):=\theta^{\prime}+t(\theta-\theta^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is (a.e.) differentiable in <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, the fundamental theorem of calculus along <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)=\int_{0}^{1}J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\,(\theta-\theta^{\prime})\,\mathrm{d}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)=\int_{0}^{1}J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\,(\theta-\theta^{\prime})\,\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Taking norms and using the operator norm,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\|J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\mathrm{d}t\;\|\Delta\theta\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\|J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\,\mathrm{d}t\;\|\Delta\theta\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">By Tonelli/Fubini to exchange expectation and integral, and Cauchy–Schwarz in <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s}\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s}\|J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}\mathrm{d}t\;\|\Delta\theta\|\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>par</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s}\|g_{\theta}(s)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(s)\|_{2}\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s}\|J_{\phi(t)}g_{\phi(t)}(s)\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}\mathrm{d}t\;\|\Delta\theta\|\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Combining with the TV inequality yields the claimed clean-value bound with factor <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha c</annotation></semantics></math>. The attacked-value bound is identical with <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{J}</annotation></semantics></math>, since Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Expected robustness gap). ‣ B.2 Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> holds for robust values with the same TV control.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 (Performance–robustness trade-off under pruning). ‣ 3.2 Performance–robustness trade-offs ‣ 3 Robustness Bounds in SA-MDPs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Decompose</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{\mathrm{atk}}(\theta^{\prime};\bar{\pi})=J(\bar{\pi})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})=\big[J(\bar{\pi})-J(\pi_{\theta})\big]+\big[J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\big]+\big[J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>atk</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{\mathrm{atk}}(\theta^{\prime};\bar{\pi})=J(\bar{\pi})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})=\big[J(\bar{\pi})-J(\pi_{\theta})\big]+\big[J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\big]+\big[J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first term is <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{\mathrm{clean}}(\theta;\bar{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>clean</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{\mathrm{clean}}(\theta;\bar{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math>. The second term is bounded by Lemma 2:
<math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\leq\alpha c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>par</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{\theta})-J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})\leq\alpha c\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{par}}(\theta,\theta^{\prime})\,\|\Delta\theta\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the third term, apply Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (SA-MDP robustness improves under pruning). ‣ 3.2 Performance–robustness trade-offs ‣ 3 Robustness Bounds in SA-MDPs ‣ Pruning Cannot Hurt Robustness: Certified Trade-offs in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> to <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\leq\alpha c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\,\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}})-\tilde{J}(\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}\!\circ\!\nu^{*})\leq\alpha c\,\tilde{L}_{\theta^{\prime}}\,\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing the bounds yields the claim.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
